  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-506696</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project&#x2019;s focus is on empowering digital movements through learning exchanges with context analysis and evaluation to create an understanding of how various regions are using digital tools for mobilization and movement building. Through exchanges, and knowledge sharing, target groups gain knowledge on how best to enhance their capacity in using digital tools to advance their struggles for a just world. This project anchors its niche on people&#x2019;s rights to exercise their freedom of expression, assembly, information andspeech, especially in the online world, and use this as a basis to increase their agency in amplifying voices, advocate for their rights and champion good governance practices. Through this, the project aims to empower digital movements, build digital communitiesand construct strong elements for fundraising.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Vietnam , Oxfam is one of the leading international, non -governmental organisation. Since 1955, Oxfam is active in Vietnam withhumanitarian interventions and started development work in the late 1980&apos;s. Today, Oxfam works in 26 provinces with people, governments and civil society to promote equality and well-being through social and economic change.</narrative>
